From 9d6fb6db5ef0ea76c61607be004d9c331c23e8e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sayzal28 <Sayzal28@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:08:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Suggest up to three public sets from the experience setup
 step
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The setup AI call now also sees the public sets as short numbered lines
("17: Boutique Hotel · Reception · Looking At Desk (modern)") and returns
suggestedSetRefs: up to three numbers, best first, or none. The routes
swap the numbers for the sets (id, name, pictures, backdrop, collection,
venue, setting) and reply with suggestedSets; unknown or repeated numbers
are dropped and logged. Still one AI call; the list adds about 6k input
tokens (329 public sets locally, built in about 0.4 s).

Public sets carry almost no use-case labels (1 of 329 locally), so the
model picks from the set names, which name the place (venue · space · view).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
